theo-pod (t-169): bound the bit readers once past the end of the input

getbits(), get9_n_lessbits() and get17_n_lessbits() compute the bytes left
as `inputBufferCurrentLength - offset` in unsigned arithmetic. Once usedBits
has gone past the end of the buffer (a truncated or corrupt frame, or an
empty AudioSpecificConfig), the difference wraps, the "enough bytes" branch
is taken and the reader loads up to 4 bytes past the buffer. Found by the
host fuzzer (ASan heap-buffer-overflow in get9_n_lessbits, from
get_audio_specific_config); regression input
tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-empty-config-read.bin.

